              "use_id": "candidate:v1:b2827d794a5746c98226560fae7900bece84b4166788085b53dfd797642f24ea",
              "entry_id": "entry:v1:b3c7ee6a88bbb3742c436dc65d50ce079515e9ffbb62c202d766156185b7a4ad",
              "invocation_context_id": "invocation:v1:7c3b3582d69215dab659697b897e7fbb5e78313a5ef18099cc6f30c7e44d5e72",
              "record_type": "finding",
              "status": "confirmed_vulnerability",
              "title": "Path traversal through archive extraction (Zip Slip) supported by source analysis",
              "summary": "A request-derived value reaches the path operand of adm-zip.extractAllTo (write) with no enforced containment (CWE-22): the request-supplied archive req.files.importFile supplies entry names that are written under the destination by adm-zip (vulnerable version, declared 0.4.7). This is a static source judgment under the declared posix assumption, not runtime exploitation, symbolic-link or filesystem-state analysis, or independent Findings Review.",
              "input_validation": "Not established from the supplied evidence.",
              "use_protection": "Path assessment: traversal vulnerable, containment none, coverage incomplete. Scanner policy: A consistent traversal answer is supported by an independent source-to-operand path with a verified adm-zip.extractAllTo binding under the declared posix assumption; no enforced containment is established. Unresolved sibling paths remain visible. This is a static judgment, not runtime exploitation, symbolic-link or filesystem-state analysis, or independent Findings Review.",
              "uncertainty": "Review the evidence for the named claim. Independent findings review and runtime confirmation have not been performed. The platform assumption is posix; Windows path semantics are not modeled. Unresolved sibling paths, if any, remain separate blocking or coverage records.",
              "recommendations": {
                "title": "Validate archive entry names before extraction",
                "actions": [
                  "At routes/index.js:270, do not extract entries from a request-supplied archive with zip.extractAllTo(extracted_path, true) unless the extractor validates entry names: upgrade adm-zip to a release that rejects names escaping the destination, or extract entry by entry.",
                  "For each entry resolve destination + entry name and require the result to stay inside the destination at a path-component boundary (a separator-bounded prefix check, not a substring test), reject absolute and '..' names, and decide how symbolic-link entries are handled.",
                  "Add a regression test with an archive containing '../' entries and assert nothing is written outside the destination."
                ],
                "example_status": "no automatic patch; no verified fix is exported"
              },
              "assessment_state": "completed"
            },
